1
00:00:00,480 --> 00:00:03,880
Why is there a tiny hole
in airplane windows?

2
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:05,600
It's on purpose.

3
00:00:06,520 --> 00:00:09,920
Each window has three
panes, and the hole is in

4
00:00:09,920 --> 00:00:10,720
the middle one.

5
00:00:11,220 --> 00:00:14,680
Up high, cabin air pushes
hard against the thin

6
00:00:14,680 --> 00:00:15,560
air outside.

7
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:19,040
The hole lets that pressure
reach the outer pane,

8
00:00:19,520 --> 00:00:22,660
so it carries the load
alone, and the middle pane

9
00:00:22,660 --> 00:00:24,320
stays ready as a backup.

10
00:00:25,340 --> 00:00:28,680
The hole also lets moisture
out, so your window

11
00:00:28,680 --> 00:00:29,920
doesn't fog up.
